<item><title>Analysts see Macky Sall backing a deal with Senegal&apos;s president</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/analysts-see-macky-sall-backing-a-deal-with-senegal-s-1631f2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/analysts-see-macky-sall-backing-a-deal-with-senegal-s-1631f2/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>Two political analysts say the former president is more likely to back Faye&apos;s coalition than to return to lead his party.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:20:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Authorities close Kanène Ndiob health post, leaving 14 000 without nearby consultations</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/authorities-close-kanene-ndiob-health-post-leaving-14-000-ccac38/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/authorities-close-kanene-ndiob-health-post-leaving-14-000-ccac38/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>The closure followed a protest by residents of 48 villages seeking the replacement of the post’s head midwife, whose care patients criticised.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:07:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/authorities-close-kanene-ndiob-health-post-leaving-14-000-ccac38/share.jpg" length="43150" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/authorities-close-kanene-ndiob-health-post-leaving-14-000-ccac38/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
